# Topic access control, least privilege.
#
# Every identity gets exactly the topics its code already uses — the read
# rules below were taken from each twin's subscriptions() method and the
# write rules from its publish calls, not guessed:
#
#   twins/cooling_twin.py:68      -> datacenter/racks/CRAC-01
#   twins/occupancy_twin.py:12    -> datacenter/occupancy/staff|workload
#   twins/energy_twin.py:15       -> datacenter/racks/+
#   twins/rack_twin.py:20         -> datacenter/racks/<own rack>
#   orchestrator/orchestrator.py  -> datacenter/twin-state/+
#
# There is no default/anonymous section: with allow_anonymous false and no
# `topic` lines outside a `user` block, an unlisted client gets nothing.
#
# THE SINGLE-WRITER RULE: `orchestrator` is the only identity in this file
# with `topic write datacenter/recommendations/room`. A recommendation is the
# system's actuating output — the thing a human acts on — so exactly one
# component may assert one. tests/test_broker_security.py case 3 proves this
# by having a twin try and fail.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- producers
user sensor-simulator
topic write datacenter/racks/SR-RACK-01
topic write datacenter/racks/SR-RACK-02
topic write datacenter/racks/SR-RACK-03
topic write datacenter/racks/CRAC-01
topic write datacenter/status/simulator

user occupancy-publisher
topic write datacenter/occupancy/staff
topic write datacenter/occupancy/workload

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sub-twins
# Each twin may publish its OWN state and status topic and nothing else, so a
# compromised twin cannot forge another twin's state into the orchestrator.
user twin-cooling
topic read  datacenter/racks/CRAC-01
topic write datacenter/twin-state/cooling
topic write datacenter/status/cooling

user twin-occupancy
topic read  datacenter/occupancy/staff
topic read  datacenter/occupancy/workload
topic write datacenter/twin-state/occupancy
topic write datacenter/status/occupancy

user twin-energy
topic read  datacenter/racks/+
topic write datacenter/twin-state/energy
topic write datacenter/status/energy

user twin-rack-SR-RACK-01
topic read  datacenter/racks/SR-RACK-01
topic write datacenter/twin-state/rack-SR-RACK-01
topic write datacenter/status/rack-SR-RACK-01

user twin-rack-SR-RACK-02
topic read  datacenter/racks/SR-RACK-02
topic write datacenter/twin-state/rack-SR-RACK-02
topic write datacenter/status/rack-SR-RACK-02

user twin-rack-SR-RACK-03
topic read  datacenter/racks/SR-RACK-03
topic write datacenter/twin-state/rack-SR-RACK-03
topic write datacenter/status/rack-SR-RACK-03

# ------------------------------------------------------------- orchestrator
# Reads every twin's state; is the sole author of predictions and
# recommendations. Note it has NO read access to raw telemetry — it is
# supposed to fuse twin state, not re-derive it from sensors.
user orchestrator
topic read  datacenter/twin-state/+
topic write datacenter/predictions/CRAC-01
topic write datacenter/recommendations/room
topic write datacenter/status/orchestrator

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ operator
# A human acknowledging a recommendation. May acknowledge; may not recommend.
user operator
topic read  datacenter/recommendations/room
topic write datacenter/acks/room

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- auditor
# Write-nothing by design: the audit sink records decisions, so it must not be
# able to author one. audit/audit_sink.py.
user auditor
topic read datacenter/predictions/+
topic read datacenter/recommendations/+
topic read datacenter/acks/+

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- viewer
# The credential the public dashboard ships with. It is embedded in
# client-side JavaScript and must be assumed public — which is acceptable
# precisely because it can write nothing at all. Anyone who reads it from the
# page source gains read access to a simulated data centre.
user viewer
topic read datacenter/twin-state/+
topic read datacenter/predictions/+
topic read datacenter/recommendations/+
topic read datacenter/status/+
